{
  "_comment": "Hand-maintained backend inference rules. A backend is reported when the weights of its matched signals reach 30; the sum (capped at 100) is its confidence. Signal types: 'link' = same-origin URL paths in the page (href/action/src and the page URL); 'param' = form field names and query parameter names; 'html' = the page HTML (including HTML comments and error output); 'source' = bodies of inline and fetched scripts (comments, variable names); 'script' = script URLs and file names; 'cookie' = names of cookies readable from JavaScript (HttpOnly cookies are invisible); 'header' = 'Name: regex' against response headers; 'global' = a JavaScript property path that exists in the page; 'host' = the page's own hostname. status: 'eol' = upstream support has ended (needs 'eol' date and 'source'), 'legacy' = an old generation that is often left unmaintained (needs 'source'), 'managed' = a BaaS / PaaS / serverless platform runs the backend, so there is no self-managed server framework to go stale; 'info' = identifies the framework or language only.",
  "reviewed": "2026-09-30",
  "backends": [
